{"resourceIdentifier":"5331","resourceName":"RE&UP BOTTLE PET RECYCLED CHIPS, FLAKES & NEXT-GEN T2T PET RECYCLED CHIPS PRODUCTION","description":"Re Up Geri Dönüşüm Sanayi Ve Ticaret A.Ş. Repet Şube (hereinafter “Re&Up”) operates in İnegöl, Bursa, pioneering textile recycling efforts by employing advanced recycling technologies. The project, RE&UP Bottle PET Recycled Chips, Flakes & Next-Gen T2T PET Recycled Chips Production (hereinafter “the Project”), focuses on transforming PET bottle waste and PET textile waste into high-quality, sustainable raw materials, namely PET flakes and PET chips.\r\nThrough the up cycling of PET waste, the project ensures that plastic materials are returned to the production cycle, fostering a circular economy and contributing to a more sustainable future.\r\nThe project employs both mechanical and thermomechanical recycling technologies to process PET flakes and superior PET chips. The recycling process involves sorting of polyester waste, mechanical shredding, melting, filtration, deep vacuum treatment, crystallization, and precision cutting. This results in high-performance granulates suitable for new textile products, extending the lifecycle of PET materials while meeting stringent quality standards.\r\nRe&Up operates as a high-capacity, scaled-up recycling facility. As the “first of its kind” in the region, the project mechanically transforms both textile and PET bottle waste into high-quality PET flakes and chips . Leveraging innovative and scalable technologies, the recycled materials are made suitable for direct reuse in the textile industry. This facility, aligned with sustainability goals, makes a valuable contribution to recycling efforts.\r\nRe&Up is committed not only to environmental sustainability but also to creating local employment opportunities, particularly for women, to promote social equity in the workforce. The Project’s forward-looking approach aims to expand recycling capacities with revenue from carbon credits , supporting Turkey’s circular economy targets and contributing to regional sustainability efforts.","location":{"latitude":40.106470,"longitude":29.500471},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2024-11-29","endExclusive":"2024-12-30","endInclusive":"2024-12-29"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"5331"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Inegöl"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Re Up Geri Dönüşüm Sanayi ve Ticaret A.Ş. Repet Şube"},{"type":"string","value":"Inegöl, Turkey"},{"type":"string","value":"+90 (530) 408 40 17"},{"type":"string","value":"ebru.ozkucuk@reandup.com"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Registered"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"32355"}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Waste handling and disposal"}]},{"code":"PROTOCOL_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"VMR0007"}]},{"code":"VALIDATOR_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Control Union Certifications Germany GmbH"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_REGISTRATION_DATE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"06/11/2025"}]},{"code":"CREDIT_PERIOD_INFO","values":[{"type":"string","value":"1st, 26/01/2024 - 25/01/2034"}]}]}],"documentGroups":[{"code":"VCS_PIPELINE_DOCUMENTS","description":"VCS Pipeline Documents","documents":[{"uri":"https://registry.verra.org/mymodule/ProjectDoc/Project_ViewFile.asp?FileID=123333&IDKEY=fiquwesdfmnk0iei23nnm435oiojnc909dsflk9809adlkmlkf170076207","documentType":"Draft Project Description","documentName":"VCS DRAFT PDMR 5531 26012024-30092024.pdf","uploadDate":"2024-11-27T11:17:05.24Z"},{"uri":"https://registry.verra.org/mymodule/ProjectDoc/Project_ViewFile.asp?FileID=123332&IDKEY=88723kjnf7kjandsaslmdv09887vaksmrmnwqkjoiuanfnfuq0q170074828","documentType":"Listing Repres